{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks everyone for being here. As we kick off this review, I want to make sure we cover the key areas before I give final approval. We all know the replacement ephemeral runner system passed the standard build-speed and failure-recovery tests in staging, which is good. But I'm looking at the draft operating policy, and I notice it allows 20 concurrent jobs, keeps build logs for 30 days, and doesn't currently specify immutable log storage or build-provenance attestations. I'd like to hear from each of you — developer productivity, site reliability, and compliance — on whether this policy is ready to publish or if there are gaps we need to address first."}
```

