{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I have a capacity concern that directly affects the concurrency limit in this policy. This morning, during an unrelated queue investigation, I measured a campaign-day burst of 28 simultaneous CI jobs. The safe production ceiling is exactly 32 concurrent jobs, and the queue should generate an alert when it exceeds 24 jobs. I haven't added these measurements to the capacity dashboard yet, so this data isn't visible to anyone else. Given that the draft policy allows only 20 concurrent jobs, we'd be throttling below observed real-world demand, and we also need to make sure the alerting threshold at 24 is documented before we publish."}
